# Everything is stored and checked out with LF endings.
#
# This is not a style preference. `hooks/post-note.sh` and `hooks/flush-spool.sh` are the reason
# this project runs on a machine with no Node, and a CRLF checkout breaks them outright: the
# shell reads `#!/bin/sh\r` and reports `bad interpreter`. The cross-platform behaviour was
# measured on Ubuntu and Alpine, and a line-ending conversion would quietly undo it for anyone
# who cloned from Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
